  "question": {
    "text": "The work function of a metal is in the range of <math> <mtext>2&nbsp;</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>eV</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>to</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>5</mtext><mtext> &nbsp;</mtext><mtext>eV</mtext></math>. Find which of the following wavelength of light cannot be used for photoelectric effect. (Consider, Planck's constant <math> <mo>=</mo><mtext>4</mtext><mo>×</mo><msup> <mtext>10</mtext> <mrow> <mo>−</mo><mtext>15</mtext></mrow> </msup> <mtext>&nbsp;eV-s</mtext> </math>, velocity of light <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>=3</mtext><mo>×</mo><msup><mtext>10</mtext><mn>8</mn></msup><mtext> </mtext><msup><mtext>m&nbsp;s</mtext><mtext>-1</mtext></msup></math>)",
